			<div class="content" id="post-content-4534323">
									

<p>I got a PM request to take a look in the draft stage and didn't have time to until now so this is my opportunity to be all 'hey I read this and my biggest issue was really just that this was <em>dull</em>'.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Not&nbsp;quite&nbsp;a&nbsp;full&nbsp;crit&nbsp;but&nbsp;some&nbsp;long&nbsp;form&nbsp;thoughts</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This is a wonderful world-building piece that really nicely sets out what the SCP is and how the Foundation's history works and the big problem is that that's all it really does? The note at the end could be a really good stinger but I zoned out well before that because this was just&#8230;really technical and really dry? There's lots of little bits that like, technically are pretty interesting developments (e.g, the unethical testing, the use of them as weapons) but it's all couched in such a dry, report-like format that reading through this is honestly a pain.</p>
<p>The worse example of this was:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5201 was the only known natural aphotic parthenogenetic mammalian species. SCP-5201 asexually reproduce between the 15th to 20th autotomic stage, during which the lower body regenerates its own upper torso via a process similar to epimorphic regeneration observed in autotomous lizards.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Like, it features so much technical language, and three different footnotes leading to even more technical language, and I just zone right out when I hit it. And at that point, you lost me as a reader :(</p>
<p>The choice to have this spanning a 400 year period here feels like a mistake? Like there's not really any meaningful growth implied between 1596 and 2019 since like, the Foundation seems to be a huge, globe spanning organisation with unlimited supplies in both cases; but like, the knowledge of the SCP doesn't increase or anything between the two points either?</p>
<p>At a fundamental level: there doesn't feel like there's actually a story here? It feels like a random collection of guff about the SCP and that doesn't interest me personally. And basically all of this and also the stuff <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rigen" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2826105); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2826105&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1583490065" alt="Rigen" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2826105)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rigen" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2826105); return false;">Rigen</a></span> mentioned led to me -1 this.</p>
</div>
